From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:38:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x: Allow 1.5 A of charging input on
 the A7 iPads

The A7 iPads' charger maximum is 1050 mA, the highest input limit
measured on an A7 when it was chosen. The ADT's charger node allows
0x960 = 2400 mA on all of them.

On an iPad mini 2 (J85), with the same D2089 charger data and a 1500 mA
maximum:
- a Mac's USB-C port, identified as a CDP, got 1500 mA (0x72). The
  battery charged at +958 mA at 93 %, 31.0 C.
- a 30 W charger on a USB-C to Lightning cable, identified as a USB-C
  source, got 1500 mA. The battery charged at +816 falling to +693 mA
  at 94 to 95 %, 30.8 to 30.6 C, over about four minutes.
- the same charger's USB-A port, identified as an Apple BrickID source,
  got 1500 mA, with the battery already full.

Raise the maximum to 1500 mA in the iPad mini 2's and the iPad Air's
shared files. The iPad Air has the same D2089 and the same ADT
allowance, but has not run at 1500 mA. A source that advertises less
still gets only what it advertises.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi  | 8 +++++---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi | 8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
index 84223920d..a886fbafe 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
@@ -154,8 +154,10 @@ pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
 	/*
 	 * The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input on every iPad Air.
 	 * The maximum here is the highest input limit measured on an A7
-	 * so far: 1050 mA (0x4e) charged a J72's battery at +279 to +423 mA
-	 * under the desktop, at 36 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run.
+	 * so far: 1500 mA (0x72) charged an iPad mini 2's battery at +958 mA
+	 * from a Mac's CDP port, at 31 C. Before that, 1050 mA (0x4e)
+	 * charged a J72's battery at +279 to +423 mA under the desktop, at
+	 * 36 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run.
 	 */
 	tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		compatible = "apple,d2089-tristar-charger";
@@ -169,7 +171,7 @@ tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
-		input-current-limit-microamp = <1050000>;
+		input-current-limit-microamp = <1500000>;
 
 		/* The charger decides when USB data may come on. */
 		port {
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
index 010eba811..d9871e397 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
@@ -110,8 +110,10 @@ pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
 	/*
 	 * The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input on every iPad mini 2 and 3.
 	 * The maximum here is the highest input limit measured on an A7
-	 * so far: 1050 mA (0x4e) charged a J72's battery at +279 to +423 mA
-	 * under the desktop, at 36 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run.
+	 * so far: 1500 mA (0x72) charged an iPad mini 2's battery at +958 mA
+	 * from a Mac's CDP port, at 31 C. Before that, 1050 mA (0x4e)
+	 * charged a J72's battery at +279 to +423 mA under the desktop, at
+	 * 36 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run.
 	 */
 	tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		compatible = "apple,d2089-tristar-charger";
@@ -125,7 +127,7 @@ tristar_charger: charger@60 {
 		interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
-		input-current-limit-microamp = <1050000>;
+		input-current-limit-microamp = <1500000>;
 
 		/* The charger decides when USB data may come on. */
 		port {
